  "scope": "Dispatch acknowledgement memory and SQLite policy over unchanged native request/proposal/attempt admission, bounded codecs, dispatch-history reads, writes, group finalization and consuming immediate transactions.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen orchestration shares native codecs/storage, lease validation and group primitives, not the migrated acknowledgement policy.",
    "Disposable corrupt SQLite fixtures restore constraints before production calls. They are not valid recovery checkpoints or new lease authority.",
    "The memory primitive validates the proposal first and returns that valid proposal for acknowledged records without request/lease validation or replacing stored state. The public VM entry still replays its original winner.",
    "Durable acknowledgement admits request, proposed terminal, attempt and bounded encodings before opening a transaction, including for completed records; these gates intentionally differ from retry reporting.",
    "Raw non-completed states retain their original branch, not new recovery admission. Pending acknowledgement retains only original lease/request/terminal checks, not new result correspondence.",
    "Public reopen cases inspect persisted member terminals separately from group visibility. A group's externally visible result may await its other members.",
    "Direct hooks model quota errors and uncertain commits/unwinds; native trigger and deferred-constraint cases exercise real rollback. No physical disk-full or power-loss experiment is claimed.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, complete host-neutral durable recovery or throughput benchmark is claimed."
  ],
